--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HIG / ADR conformance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • SwiftUI-native, adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): ScrollView column (maxWidth 760,
    centered on wide), ViewThatFits for the sync bar + avatar/details (horizontal ⇄ stacked).
  • Tokens only (P2): Color.TS.* / Font.TS.* / TSSpacing / TSRadius; glass via TSGlassPanel
    (.regularMaterial, ADR-005). No hardcoded colors/typography.
  • State-holder driven (ADR-004): @Observable TeslaAccountPageModel over the P1/S8 seam;
    zero networking/business logic in the view body. Telemetry view.opened once (P1/S11).
  • 4 data states implemented for the one data source: loading / empty / error / success.
    No live SSE — the profile is a query+mutation, not a stream — so no >2min staleness chip
    is applicable (ADR-013 scoped to live sources).
  • i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal via the TeslaAccountStrings facade → table
    "TeslaAccountPage"; zero hardcoded English in code; web key names preserved.
  • a11y (ADR-015): .isHeader on title/panel-title; combined VoiceOver summaries (sync bar,
    profile card, KV rows, avatar alt); Dynamic Type (system fonts); reduce-motion via
    TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton/ProgressView; light/dark/increased-contrast via dynamic tokens;
    ≥44pt primary button.
  • Units (P1/S5): no non-SI compute/store; dates formatted at the display boundary
    (TeslaAccountDateFormat — web formatDateTime / formatRelative incl. the 7-day cutoff).

